rule snap_asset_limit with provenance "USDA SNAP FY 2024 cost-of-living adjustments":
the snap asset limit of a household is an amount if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2023-10-01 <= D
    and the snap household of the household has elderly or disabled member
        and the snap asset limit elderly or disabled member is the amount
        otherwise the household is a household
        and the snap asset limit other households is the amount.

scenario standard_deduction_for_one_person_household is, as stated in "sources/us/policies/usda/snap/fy-2024-cola/deductions.test.yaml" at case 1:
    household_1 is a household.
    the calculation date is 2024-01-01.
    the household size of household_1 is 1.
    q_snap_standard_deduction expects answers ["the snap standard deduction of household_1 is 198"].
    q_snap_standard_deduction_48_states_dc expects answers ["the snap standard deduction 48 states dc of household_1 is 198"].

